WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.670
Yesterday I carried two heavy

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.330
bags to the supermarket door.

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.960
It slid open before I touched it.

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:08.930
Nobody pressed a button.

5
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:10.940
So what noticed me?

6
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.290
Let's find out.

7
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.110
Today: machines that notice, and how

8
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.990
they turn the world into numbers.

9
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.380
You notice the world with your senses.

10
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.240
Machines notice it with sensors.

11
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.530
A sensor notices just one thing,

12
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.170
like light, heat or movement.

13
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.070
Then the sensor turns what it

14
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.890
notices into a number.

15
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.750
A thermometer notices heat and

16
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.970
says thirty-one degrees.

17
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.440
That number is called a reading.

18
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.380
Many sensors copy one of your senses.

19
00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.370
A camera sees, like your eyes.

20
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.750
A microphone hears, like your ears.

21
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.900
A thermometer feels heat, like your skin.

22
00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.420
And a smoke alarm smells

23
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.000
smoke, like your nose.

24
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.800
Machines also notice things you can't.

25
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.080
A compass feels the Earth's magnetism.

26
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.280
A car's parking sensor measures

27
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.000
distance with sound too high to hear.

28
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.370
A forehead thermometer reads

29
00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.910
heat without touching.

30
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:18.560
Quick check!

31
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.110
Musa's family cooks on a charcoal

32
00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.070
stove indoors, with the door shut.

33
00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.150
Which danger can only a sensor notice?

34
00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.510
A gas with no colour or

35
00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.450
smell: carbon monoxide.

36
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.680
Charcoal or a generator burning in a

37
00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.160
closed room makes it, and it can kill.

38
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.580
Only an alarm can notice it.

39
00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.060
So run generators outside, and

40
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.960
never burn charcoal indoors.

41
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.910
Back to the supermarket door.

42
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.770
Sense: a motion sensor above it

43
00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.910
notices something moving close by.

44
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.690
Decide: a tiny computer follows its

45
00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.450
rule, if someone is close, open.

46
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.920
Act: a motor slides the door open.

47
00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.330
These three steps are all around you.

48
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.240
A street light senses

49
00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.260
darkness and switches on.

50
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.020
A hand dryer senses your hands and blows.

51
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.520
A fridge senses it's warming

52
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.100
up, and cools again.

53
00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.830
Not everything with a switch senses.

54
00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.190
A torch you switch on senses nothing:

55
00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.030
you noticed the dark and decided.

56
00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.840
A microphone takes sound in: it senses.

57
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.720
A loudspeaker sends sound out: it acts.

58
00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:41.830
Your turn.

59
00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.870
Our school's water tank has a sensor

60
00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.970
that notices how full it is.

61
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.710
When it reads low, the pump starts.

62
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.780
Which part decided?

63
00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.760
A small computer, following a rule,

64
00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.840
decided: the sensor only noticed,

65
00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.880
and the pump only acted.

66
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.930
Remember: a sensor notices one

67
00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.630
thing and gives a number.

68
00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.550
Machines sense what you can't.

69
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.220
And smart devices sense, decide and act.

70
00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.230
Try it tomorrow: go on a sensor hunt at

71
00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.550
home, at school and on the way.

72
00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.440
Find things that switch by themselves.

73
00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.360
For each, write what it senses,

74
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.080
what decides and what it does.

75
00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.990
Next time: your phone's sensors.
